Vikram and Betal: The Honest Servant

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a king who had a very loyal servant,” said Betal. “The servant was known for his honesty.”

One day, the king lost his precious necklace.

He asked all the servants about it, but no one knew anything.

The king became worried.

The honest servant stepped forward and said, “Your Majesty, I will help you find it.”

He searched everywhere in the palace.

Finally, he found the necklace in the garden.

He brought it back to the king without taking anything.

The king was very happy and rewarded him.

But some people said, “He found the necklace, maybe he had hidden it.”

The king smiled and said, “A truly honest person does not need to prove himself again and again.”

Betal then asked, “Vikram, why did the king trust the servant?”

Vikram replied, “Because true honesty is shown through actions.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Honesty is proven through actions.
